{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-run-panel-forms-a-01","date":"2026-11-24","lens":"15","surface":"panel","area":"panel/forms","refs":["F-panel-421","F-panel-401","F-panel-414","FN-L5-panel-auth-data-01"],"severity":"S3","title":"When money or a member taken with no internet is refused by the server later, MettleUp is never told","what":"A payment, sale or new member saved at the desk with no internet waits on that computer and is sent when the internet is back. If the server then refuses it (for example more than the member now owes, or too old), it is marked as not sent and kept on that one computer, with a warning bar for the desk. The reason is written only in that browser's hidden log. Nothing reaches MettleUp, so cash with a printed receipt that never reached the gym's records stays invisible to us until the owner notices and complains.","expected":"Each refused offline item sends one short report to MettleUp (the kind of item and the refusal reason, no names or phone numbers), so a pattern of refusals is seen before a gym tells us.","evidence":["apps/dashboard/src/crm/data/cloud.ts:795-812","apps/dashboard/src/crm/crashReport.ts:66-81"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"refused-offline-work-never-reported","who":"owners and front desk","how_often":"every refused offline item","fix_line":"Send a short report to MettleUp each time the server refuses something the desk saved offline","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-run-panel-forms-a-02","date":"2026-11-24","lens":"6","surface":"panel","area":"panel/forms","refs":["F-panel-401","F-panel-414","F-panel-406"],"severity":"S3","title":"The nightly backup has never been restored from a real night's copy","what":"Every desk payment, sale and member is in the nightly backup, and the automatic checks restore a copy of test data on every code change. The written plan also asks for a restore of a real night's copy onto the test server once after switching on and once mid-pilot, with the result written down. No such result is recorded anywhere, three weeks after backups went live. So nobody knows that a real copy (real size, real sign-in accounts) can be brought back, or how long it takes.","expected":"A real night's copy is restored onto the test server, the gym totals are compared, and the date and result are written down; then again mid-pilot.","evidence":["docs/BACKUP-RESTORE.md:3","docs/BACKUP-RESTORE.md:13","docs/BACKUP-RESTORE.md:37-56","PROGRESS.md:87"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"real-backup-restore-never-drilled","who":"every gym","how_often":"once, on the day a restore is needed","fix_line":"Run the written restore drill on the test server with last night's copy and record the result","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
